0029: the survey writes itself to the boot stick

The -v console was the survey's only channel and it is gone before the boot finishes, so a
survey could not be carried back. With navi48-survey-report=1 the kext formats the facts the
survey already read (identity, BAR5, VRAM, IP discovery, firmware choice, IP versions and
segment bases, DCN allowlist verdict, geometry, PSP state, requested stage) into the fixed
1536-byte record in NAVI48.TXT, through the same mounted-volume / raw-FAT channels patch
0027/0028 built for the verdict. The mounted volume is tried first for 30 s before the block
device, so diskarbitrationd's mount wins whenever it is coming. The report adds no hardware
access: it is a record of reads the boot already performed. Host suite covers the formatter,
the cap contract and the realistic worst case (ten IP rows, fifteen segments each) staying
inside 1536 bytes.
